      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've seen similar reports to Ghostt's findings, but at the same time this isn't something that needs to be \"implemented\" into VR-Chat, all that's needed is to contact Nvidia to get added to the list of applications in the driver.\nEven so, I've personally got very little interest in this tech for VR-Chat until it can do the reverse and offer performance enhancements rather than image quality enhancements at the cost of performance. I run VRC on a Ryz-3700x and a RTX-2070-Super, and whilst it handles the game beautifully, I'm still in re-projection mode far more often than I ever see 90 or 120fps. VR-Chat isn't really an application that benefits much from super sampling, and nor does it have the performance breathing space to make practical use of it, even on some of the best machines.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
